e from initialization. Here the top row, bottom row and left/right edge columns hold some of the largest, most coherent weights in the network, so the objects routinely touch all four borders. That rules out the digit/character datasets.\n- The specific patterns fit clothing silhouettes scaled to fill the frame: a top row with two shoulder blobs and a differently-treated neckline/centre; sleeves reaching the left and right edges in the upper half; a bottom row with two \"legs\" separated by an empty centre (trousers) versus a solid centre hem (dresses/coats) versus a long flat band toward the right edge (shoe soles/heels); wide objects (shoes, bags) touching the left edge in the middle rows. Fashion-MNIST's preprocessing (longest side resized to 28 px, then centred) produces exactly this border-touching layout, and its class set (tops with sleeves, trousers, dresses, three kinds of footwear, bags) matches the detectors seen.\n\n**Dataset:** Fashion-MNIST (Zalando 28×28 grayscale clothing article images).\n\n**Classes:** 0 T-shirt/top, 1 Trouser, 2 Pullover, 3 Dress, 4 Coat, 5 Sandal, 6 Shirt, 7 Sneaker, 8 Bag, 9 Ankle boot.\n\n**Confidence:** 85%",
